fact WorkItem(id: "WI-501", description: some(value: "Persistence (term_ser): a serialize -> reload round-trip DROPS none()-valued Option fields, so the reloaded term has FEWER named args than the source-loaded form and silently fails to hash-cons / discrim-match it. Same hazard class as WI-498/WI-433 (silent never-match) but about field PRESENCE, not field ORDER. MECHANISM: the serialize side (term_to_value, persistence/term_ser.rs:601-604) emits a field only when its value != JSON null, i.e. it SKIPS none()-valued Option fields ('Skip none() values (Option absent)'). The deserialize side (load_entry, term_ser.rs ~290-313) builds named_args ONLY from the JSON keys PRESENT and then make_entity_term — it does NOT backfill the entity's declared-but-absent fields. By contrast the source loader's convert_term DOES expand partial named args (load.rs:5259-5279: fills missing declared fields, with fresh vars). So a source-loaded fact carries ALL declared fields (the persisted workitems.anthill writes 'context: none, generates: none, requires_capability: none' EXPLICITLY => 8 present args), but the same fact serialized->reloaded comes back with only the non-none fields (e.g. 5 args) => a structurally DIFFERENT Term::Fn => distinct TermId => never unifies with a pattern/fact loaded from source. Round-trip is also non-idempotent. PROVEN-ADJACENT: surfaced during WI-498 review; WI-498 fixed field-ORDER canonicalization, this is the orthogonal field-PRESENCE gap on the same boundary. DECISION NEEDED (pick one, loud-error principle in mind): (a) serialize emits none() explicitly (stop skipping null) so JSON carries every declared field — simplest, keeps the store self-describing, but bloats output with nones; (b) deserialize backfills absent DECLARED fields with none() (Option fields) at load_entry via entity_field_names, matching how source facts carry explicit none() and making round-trip idempotent + discrim-matchable — note the source loader fills missing with FRESH VARS which is wrong for a GROUND persisted fact, so don't blindly copy that; none() is the right ground fill for absent Option fields. Consider non-Option missing fields too (likely a loud error: a required field absent from the store is corruption, not a fresh var). ACCEPTANCE: an entity with a none()-valued Option field, serialized then reloaded, yields a term that hash-cons-matches the source-loaded form (and round-trip is idempotent); cargo-test green."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-06-17T07:37:11Z"))

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-501", author: "user", content: "PREMISE CORRECTION + DELIVERED 2026-06-17. The filed premise (serializer DROPS none() fields -> backfill) was WRONG: a written none loads as Term::Ref(anthill.prelude.Option.none), term_to_value rendered it (and every nullary entity / enum variant Ref) to a bare SHORT-NAME string and stripped some(value:x)->x, while reload rebuilt strings as Const(String)/Fn — so a serialize->reload round-trip hash-cons-matched the source for almost NO field. User chose TYPE-DIRECTED DESERIALIZATION. FIX (both sides, term_ser.rs): SERIALIZE: term_to_value Ref(Option.none) -> JSON null so the entity-field loop DROPS it (absent encodes none); json_to_toml null -> LOUD Err (was silent null->empty-string, which corrupted none-inside-a-list via TOML). RELOAD: load_entry threads each field's DECLARED type (entity_field_types) into value_to_term_typed — Option[T=U]: null/absent -> none()=Ref(Option.none), present -> some(value: recurse U); List[T=U] -> build_cons_list of typed elems (canonical List.cons/nil, falls back to interned short names when prelude absent so schema-less loads don't panic like KB::build_list); entity/enum sort + string -> Ref(variant resolved <qualified-sort>.<name>); object {Variant:payload} -> typed ctor (recursing field types); nullary entities rebuilt as Ref (was Fn) to match loader. backfill_absent_fields: absent Option -> none(), absent required -> LOUD SerError::MissingField. option_none_ref/some_wrap build EXACT loader forms; type_head_and_inner extracts head sort + inner T. Old untyped fns replaced by _typed family; schema-less entities keep untyped path (ty=None) so prior behavior preserved. /code-review xhigh: acted on 3 in-scope findings (TOML null loud-error; reload null-in-non-Option loud-error; String-typed value no longer mis-resolved to a global entity Ref — declared type is authoritative). Residual NARROW gaps (nested-Option some(none()) collapse; serialize short-name dispatch asymmetry; foreign positional-payload never-match) filed as WI-503. TESTS (github_todo_test.rs): wi501_workitem_round_trips_through_store (full WorkItem some/none/nullary/empty-list hash-cons-matches source; VERIFIED fails if serialize none-drop reverted) + wi501_missing_required_field_errors_loudly. Full workspace green (56 binaries, 2024 tests). Rebased onto origin/main (WI-id collision: remote independently filed a different WI-502, so this residual ticket = WI-503).", at: "2026-06-17T07:37:10Z")
